&lt;p&gt;The Senior Solutions Architect, Partnerships will work within our Go-To-Market team and be dedicated to our Partnerships business unit, focused on the 0-to-1 market opportunities that the BU pursues, most notably our current effort to expand into the automotive lending space. As a consultative product expert, you&#39;ll help clients unlock business value while collaborating with the Account Team, Product, Engineering, and Data Science teams throughout the customer journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a 0-to-1 role at its core. You&#39;ll operate in an environment where the product, ideal customer profile, ideal use case, and sales motion are not yet fully defined, and you&#39;ll help define them. While you&#39;ll support both pre-sales and post-sales, this role carries a strong bias toward pre-sales, partnering closely with Account Executives to shape and advance new deals in an emerging market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll engage with our U.S. customer base of large financial institutions, as well as key technology and platform players within the financial space. Many of our strategic partnerships are Business-to-Business-to-Consumer in nature, so you&#39;ll own the technology and product aspects of these relationships, including both the partner integrations themselves and the end-customer implementations served through the platform. A working familiarity with HTML, JavaScript, RESTful APIs, and scripting languages such as Python will be essential for demonstrating the value of Nova Credit&#39;s platform to customers and prospects. You don&#39;t need to be a full-stack engineer, but you should be comfortable reading HTML, making light edits, and speaking credibly to technical stakeholders. Your contributions will be critical to the company&#39;s overall success!&lt;/p&gt;
